/* ---------- java.util collections core ----------
 * One object model for java.util maps, sets, lists, queues and deques with
 * the Java contracts: keys and elements compare through equals()/hashCode()
 * (String and the primitive wrappers natively, every other object through a
 * virtual call so app overrides apply), sorted collections order through
 * Comparable/Comparator, and iteration follows the collection's encounter
 * order. ETD2X never reclaims Java objects, so iterators are live cursors
 * over the backing store and hold no per-element references, and map views
 * and entry nodes are created once per map/entry. */

